/// Sched module — one-shot scheduler primitives (Plan 442 A5)
///
/// The render-loop timer port: `set_timeout(callback, delay_ms)` schedules a
/// single delayed callback and returns a handle; `clear_timeout(handle)`
/// cancels it. This is the Auto surface of the auto-down SchedulerTimer
/// contract (`setTimeout(fn, ms)` / `clearTimeout(handle)` — batch/typewriter
/// streaming cadence); the callback fires on the render loop's timer tick,
/// so unlike `time.sleep_ms` nothing blocks the engine thread.
///
/// The callback takes two forms:
/// - a closure value (by-value captures only): `set_timeout(() => { ... }, 16)`
/// - a widget event-name string: `set_timeout("Refresh", 16)` (dispatched
///   like any UI event — the `.Tick`-adjacent form for handler bodies).

/// Schedule a one-shot timer; returns the timer id handle.
pub fn set_timeout(callback fn(), delay_ms int) int;

/// Cancel a pending one-shot timer; returns whether a timer was removed.
pub fn clear_timeout(timer_id int) bool;
